            "title": "Should airlines be worried about earnings hit from US shutdown?",
            "description": "<p>A record 31 million Americans are expected to take to the skies and <a data-i13n=\"cpos:1;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/traveling-thanksgiving-consider-travel-rewards-194500190.html\">travel this week for Thanksgiving</a>, according to Airlines for America's data, as major airline operators recover from <a data-i13n=\"cpos:2;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/video/airlines-time-smooth-following-govt-220000861.html\">the US government shutdown.</a></p>\n<p>Bloomberg Intelligence senior aerospace defense and airlines industry analyst George Ferguson joins Market Catalysts to comment on whether this current quarter's flight disruptions due to the shutdown may materialize in airline earnings.</p>\n<p>To watch more expert insights and analysis on the latest market action, check out more\u00a0<a data-i13n=\"cpos:3;pos:1\" href=\"https://finance.yahoo.com/videos/series/market-catalysts/\">Market Catalysts</a>.</p>",
